-- ============================================================================
-- The seeded library, REBUILT 2026-08-20 (global rows, user_id IS NULL)
--
-- Supersedes 20260815120300's 25-exercise seed, which stays frozen as history.
-- Drake reviewed a 310-name list and this is the result: generic names dropped
-- in favour of equipment-specific ones ("Lat Pulldown" -> Cable / Machine),
-- duplicates merged, Hammer Strength named the way every other variant already
-- is. Safe to rebuild wholesale because NO workout history existed yet —
-- verified by dumping the project's data, not assumed.
--
-- GENERATED FILE — do not edit by hand.
--   source: MCPStrength/MCPStrength/Resources/{exercise,measurement}-seed.json
--   regenerate: python3 supabase/scripts/generate_library_seed.py
--
-- These rows are the integrity constraint for the whole product. Without a
-- shared library with stable ids, every AI-generated plan invents its own
-- exercise names and a user's history for one movement fragments across
-- "Lateral Raise (Machine)" / "Machine Lateral Raise" / "Lat Raise" — and
-- progress tracking, the entire point, silently breaks.
--
-- THE UUIDS ARE A PERMANENT CONTRACT. They are baked into the seed JSON and
-- copied here verbatim; they are never generated at apply time. Every workout
-- ever logged points at an exercise by id, so a re-seed that hands an existing
-- exercise a NEW uuid detaches every user's history for that movement. There
-- is no good fix afterwards.
--
-- The upserts refresh only the LIBRARY-DEFINED fields (name, body_part,
-- secondary_body_parts, category, aliases), matching ExerciseSeedImporter on
-- the device. Per-user settings live in exercise_preferences and are never
-- touched by a re-seed.
-- ============================================================================

-- 301 exercises
on conflict (id) do update set
  name                 = excluded.name,
  body_part            = excluded.body_part,
  secondary_body_parts = excluded.secondary_body_parts,
  category             = excluded.category,
  aliases              = excluded.aliases,
  deleted_at           = null;


-- 10 retired exercises — TOMBSTONED, not deleted
--
-- A hard delete cannot reach a device that was offline when it happened, so
-- the row returns on that device's next pull. Setting deleted_at travels like
-- any other edit and every @Query in the app already filters it out.
-- AGENTS.md rule 1.
--
-- `updated_at` is bumped so last-write-wins actually prefers the tombstone
-- over whatever timestamp the row is carrying locally.
-- Barbell Row -> Bent Over Row (Barbell)
-- Dumbbell Row -> Bent Over Row (Dumbbell)
-- Lat Pulldown -> Cable / Machine, no alias (two successors)
-- Seated Cable Row -> Seated Row (Cable)
-- Leg Extension -> Leg Extension (Machine)
-- Leg Curl (Machine) -> Lying / Seated, no alias (two successors)
-- Triceps Pushdown (Cable) -> Straight Bar / Rope, no alias (two successors)
-- Dip -> Triceps Dip
-- Assisted Pull Up -> Pull Up (Assisted)
-- Assisted Dip -> Triceps Dip (Assisted)
update public.exercises
set deleted_at = now(), updated_at = now()
where user_id is null
  and deleted_at is null
  and id in (
    '5b3e00a2-b1bf-470e-9782-408984ab130e',
    '94bdcb4a-9469-448d-af17-b62e68f1abb5',
    '07fc8389-e0d3-45d3-af79-4dd97d777bd2',
    'a7d8825a-ed41-49c8-9c49-406db9ea9a36',
    '32b233a3-6633-4d88-94b7-15869ad6fc82',
    '7c4b861c-40ef-4b09-a6f8-25335ad18495',
    '0f13df5a-edf6-4935-a7dc-a3f08ac6298c',
    'f32d2257-6616-4b8e-9dbc-2765293a6e50',
    '23ba51e7-0b8d-44ba-9a95-f55a6389af0c',
    'e3e0ddfb-5f39-4a21-ad26-c8f146c5f355'
  );


-- 18 measurement types
--
-- The seed JSON also carries a `unit` per type. There is no column for it:
-- MeasurementType has no unit in the SwiftData model either — the unit is
-- recorded per ENTRY, because a user can switch units and the entries already
-- written keep the unit they were taken in. The JSON field seeds the default
-- offered in the UI, which is a client concern.
on conflict (id) do update set
  name       = excluded.name,
  group_kind = excluded.group_kind,
  sort_order = excluded.sort_order;
